# Trivy ignore file
# Known false positives / accepted risks for container image scanning.
# Format: one CVE ID per line. Lines starting with '#' are comments.
# Each entry MUST include a comment explaining why it is suppressed.
# Review this file regularly and remove entries once no longer applicable.
#
# Documentation: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/

# Example entries (uncomment and adjust as needed):

# CVE-2023-00000
#   False positive: vulnerability reported in a package that is not present
#   in the final image (removed during multi-stage build). Verified via
#   `trivy image --scanners vuln <image>` and manual inspection.

# CVE-2023-00001
#   Accepted risk: low-impact issue in a transitive dependency with no
#   available fix upstream. Tracked in issue #XXXX; revisit when a patched
#   version is released.
